<%#
  Hero stats — 4 numbers, read off the deployed mainnet program. The
  `measured` record in show.html.erb says which version, slot and date;
  the line under the grid prints it, because the numbers are presented as
  facts (the version pill above reads the committed IDL, not this record).

  TWO DISTINCTIONS THIS GRID MUST NOT BLUR:
    - the DEPLOYED FILE is deployed_file_bytes. elf_content_bytes is the
      logical ELF content inside it and is labeled as such, nothing else.
    - what the account HOLDS (locked_sol, funded at funded_rate) is not what
      it would COST today (pd_min_sol, queried at measured[:slot]).

    locals: locked_sol, pd_min_sol, float_sol, buffer_sol, deployed_file_bytes,
            elf_content_bytes, programdata_space, funded_rate, current_rate,
            v015_perm_sol, measured
%>
<section class="mb-8">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3 sm:gap-4">

    <div class="card p-4 sm:p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] sm:text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-2">Deployed program</div>
      <div class="font-mono text-2xl sm:text-3xl tabular-nums text-heading leading-tight">
        <%= number_with_delimiter(deployed_file_bytes) %><span class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-secondary ml-1">bytes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs text-muted mt-2 leading-snug" data-test="contract-elf-content">
        ~<%= (deployed_file_bytes / 1024.0).round %> KB. The file the loader wrote, read through its last byte.
        <span data-test="contract-elf-content-bytes"><%= number_with_delimiter(elf_content_bytes) %></span>
        bytes of it are logical ELF content; the rest is zero padding.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-4 sm:p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] sm:text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-2">Locked in ProgramData</div>
      <div class="font-mono text-2xl sm:text-3xl tabular-nums text-warning leading-tight" data-test="contract-locked-sol">
        <%= sprintf("%.3f", locked_sol) %><span class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-secondary ml-1">SOL</span>
      </div>
      <div class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs text-muted mt-2 leading-snug">
        <%
          delta = locked_sol - v015_perm_sol
          delta_word = delta >= 0 ? "more" : "less"
        %>
        What the account holds today, funded at <%= number_with_delimiter(funded_rate) %> lamports a byte.
        <%= sprintf("%.2f SOL %s than v0.15.1's %.3f", delta.abs, delta_word, v015_perm_sol) %>, funded at that same rate.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-4 sm:p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] sm:text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-2">Refundable buffer</div>
      <div class="font-mono text-2xl sm:text-3xl tabular-nums text-mint leading-tight">
        <%= sprintf("%.3f", buffer_sol) %><span class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-secondary ml-1">SOL</span>
      </div>
      <div class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs text-muted mt-2 leading-snug">
        A buffer holding the same <%= number_with_delimiter(deployed_file_bytes) %>-byte file. Refunded once <code class="font-mono text-secondary">close-buffer</code> runs.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card p-4 sm:p-5">
      <div class="text-[10px] sm:text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-semibold mb-2">Float to deploy today</div>
      <div class="font-mono text-2xl sm:text-3xl tabular-nums text-primary leading-tight">
        ~<%= sprintf("%.2f", float_sol) %><span class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-secondary ml-1">SOL</span>
      </div>
      <%# Names the ROLE, not a key. The buffer rent is paid by the keypair that
          runs write-buffer, and upgrades execute through the Squads multisig,
          where Xan (the server bot) holds no mainnet seat. See docs/SOLANA.md,
          the Membership and threshold paragraph. %>
      <div class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs text-muted mt-2 leading-snug" data-test="contract-float-holder">
        Both accounts exist at once during a deploy. Needed in the deploying wallet before write-buffer.
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
  <p class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs text-muted mt-3 leading-snug break-words"
     data-test="contract-measured-on"
     data-version="<%= measured[:version] %>"
     data-idl-sha256="<%= measured[:idl_sha256] %>">
    Measured on turf-vault v<%= measured[:version] %>, as deployed on <%= measured[:cluster] %>,
    at slot <%= number_with_delimiter(measured[:slot]) %> (<%= measured[:date] %>).
    Program sha256 <code class="font-mono text-secondary"><%= measured[:program_sha256] %></code>
    &mdash; check it with <code class="font-mono text-secondary">solana program dump</code> and <code class="font-mono text-secondary">shasum -a 256</code>.
    Rent is a snapshot, not a constant: this account's <%= number_with_delimiter(programdata_space) %> bytes were funded at
    <%= number_with_delimiter(funded_rate) %> lamports a byte, and at that slot the cluster's rent-exempt minimum
    priced them at <%= number_with_delimiter(current_rate) %> a byte
    (<span data-test="contract-pd-min-sol"><%= sprintf("%.3f", pd_min_sol) %></span> SOL), a rate it keeps lowering.
  </p>
</section>
